  "verified": false,
  "notes": "One set issued in two waves. Topps numbers it 1-700 but prints #364 and #565 as holding no card, so the base checklist has 698 rows across the two ranges.",
  "provenance": [
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: 2018-Topps-BB-Series-1-Checklist.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 1 (#1-350) and its inserts",
      "notes": "Four base cards are tailed \"World Series\" for the 2017 Series, the earliest printed form of the designation this repo records as WSH; later years print \"World Series Highlights\"."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: 2018-Topps-Baseball-Series-2-Checklist.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 2 (#351-700) and its inserts",
      "notes": "Topps prints \"364DOES NOT EXIST IN SERIES 2\" and the same for #565, so those two numbers hold no card and the base checklist is 698 rows over a 700-number range. Both lines are set in full caps and read as section headers, which split the base run into sections named after themselves before the converter learned to recognise them; they are now reported as absent numbers and get no row. The series ranges in series[] are the numbering Topps used, not a count. Five sections headed AUTOGRAPH PARALLEL or AUTOGRAPH VARIATION share no card number with any other file here, so each is an autograph checklist numbering itself."
    }
  ]
